EP:01 How js works and execution context.

Everything in javascript happens inside execution context. Excecution context is a container where the whole javascript is executed. It is like a big box having two components in it. 
 a. Memory component: Where all the variables and functions are stored as key/value pairs. It is also called as variavle environment.
 b. Code component: It is the space where all the code is executed one line at a time. Its also known as Thread of execution.

Javascript is a sigle threaded synchronous language.

EP:02 How javascript code is executed and call stack.
The execution context is created in two phases.
 a. Memory creation phase: JS engine (V8 in Google Chrome) allocates memory to all the variables and functions.
 b. Code execution phase: The whole code is executed one line at a time. This execution is managed by call stack. Global execution context is pushed to bottom of the stack. Call stack maintains the order of the execution.
 Call stack is also known as Execution context stack, Program stack, Control stack, Runtime stack, Machine stack. 

