EP:08 What is a temporal dead zone?
-> Temporal dead zone is the time since the let/const variable is hoisted and till it is initialized some value.

Are let & const declarations hoisted? -> Yes let and const are hoisted in different way than var. These are in temporal dead zone for time being. 

Difference among SyntaxError, ReferenceError & TypeError?


ReferenceError: Cannot access a1 befor initialization.

In case of let, we can not delcare a variable again, it gives SyntaxError and js will not execute a single line of code.

SynatxError: Identifier 'a1' has already been declared at {.js line no}

const is more strict than let. We can not initalize const later after its declaration. Otherwise shows SyntaxError:

SyntaxError: Missing initlizer in const declaration.

Recommendations: Tries to use 'const' first if possible, otherwise let be they have temporal deadzone. Avoid using var anymore.

To avoid temporal dead zone, push every declaration and initialization on the top.

